{"node_id":"NRS_484B_153_2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-153-2"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"d1","text":"A person","role":"subject"},{"id":"d2","text":"shall not open the door of or board or alight from","role":"obligation"},{"id":"d3","text":"the side of a vehicle which is closest to passing traffic","role":"condition"},{"id":"d4","text":"in such a manner as to interfere with","role":"standard"},{"id":"d5","text":"moving vehicular traffic.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"d1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"The person who opens a door, boards or alights is not observable as such; the conduct is the door of a vehicle opening, so the rule judges the vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose door it is. Same words mapped to the vehicle aggregate by LVMC_11_22_010."},{"span":"d2","atoms":["sig.door_open"],"derived":[],"justification":"sig.door_open: 'a door open; side ∈ {traffic, curb}'. Opening the door, boarding and alighting through that side all show as the door on that side being open."},{"span":"d3","atoms":["sig.door_open","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the side of a vehicle which is closest to passing traffic' is the value side = traffic of sig.door_open; the vehicle is the subject (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle)."},{"span":"d5","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'vehicular traffic': road users that are traffic (admitted DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, 'vehicles and other conveyances … using any highway for purposes of travel') and vehicles (DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle); 'moving': not at rest, the negation of drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation')."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"d4","standard":"in such a manner as to interfere with","concepts":["rel.contact","rel.longitudinal_overlap","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.door_swing_reach"],"convention":"While the traffic-side door is open, a moving vehicle of the traffic is interfered with where it touches the subject (rel.contact) or passes alongside it (rel.longitudinal_overlap: the two projections on the subject's heading share length) with a lateral body gap (rel.surface_gap, lateral component) no greater than the lateral reach of an open side door, p.door_swing_reach: it then drives through the space the open door takes.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a vehicle and its door on the side closest to passing traffic is open (sig.door_open side traffic).","obligation":"No road user c that is traffic and a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and not at rest (not drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance) is in contact with the subject (rel.contact), or alongside it (rel.longitudinal_overlap: projections share length) with the lateral component of rel.surface_gap(subject, c) at most p.door_swing_reach; violated where one is.","params":["p.door_swing_reach","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"d1","why":"'A person' who opens the door, boards or alights is read through the vehicle's traffic-side door being open: who is at the door is not observable.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"d2","why":"Boarding and alighting are read through the open traffic-side door they pass through; boarding or alighting from a vehicle side that has no door is not read.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"d4","why":"Interference is read as a moving vehicle touching the subject or passing alongside within the open door's reach; a moving vehicle that brakes or swerves earlier to avoid the door is not read.","kind":"reading"}]