centre line l lying on that highway (st.centre_line, st.on_way): prim.region_lateral_offset(l, subject) is at least half the subject's full width (kin.extent) less p.lateral_position_tolerance, or the subject's body is within p.lateral_position_tolerance of a road edge (st.road_edge, st.region_geometry distance) lying on its right (prim.region_lateral_offset negative). Violated where neither holds.","params":["p.oncoming_heading_cos","p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.meeting_horizon","p.lateral_position_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"h1","why":"'Drivers' is read through the vehicles' controlled motion, whoever or whatever controls them.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"h5","why":"'the paved portion of the highway' is read as the roadway the centre line divides; a paved shoulder is not added to either half. Its half is given while the other vehicle approaches within p.meeting_horizon or is alongside.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"h6","why":"'as nearly as possible' is read through the subject's room to its right road edge; obstacles on the subject's half are not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Two-lane two-way road; the moving subject car straddles the centre line by 1 m while an oncoming car approaches 2 s away, with 2 m of room to its right road edge."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same road; the subject car keeps its body right of the centre line as the oncoming car passes."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject car drives on a highway whose lane counts two lanes in its direction."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Two-lane road with an oncoming car approaching; the source maps regions without their outline (st.region_geometry absent), so the offset from the centre line is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject car drives over the centre line on a two-lane road with no other vehicle in the scene."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A very narrow paved road; the subject's body crosses the centre line by 0.5 m while its right side is at the road edge, as an oncoming car passes."}],"literals":[{"span":"h4","text":"one","value":1,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.oncoming_heading_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle off exactly opposed headings (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as proceeding in opposite directions","source":"heading tolerance of road-geometry alignment; lane-change heading angles"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of the acquisition source"},{"name":"p.meeting_horizon","unit":"s","value":5.0,"convention":"the time ahead within which two vehicles closing head-on on a narrow two-way road count as meeting, so that each keeps to its half: the decision-and-steering time of a driver adjusting lateral position","source":"AASHTO decision sight distance (avoidance manoeuvre times)"},{"name":"p.lateral_position_tolerance","unit":"m","value":0.3,"convention":"the lateral margin within which a vehicle body counts as at a line or an edge: lane-keeping variability of a driven vehicle plus the source's position error","source":"lane-keeping lateral deviation studies"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_208_1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-208-1"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"k1","text":"Except as otherwise provided in subsection 2,","role":"exception"},{"id":"k2","text":"on a controlled-access highway","role":"condition"},{"id":"k3","text":"which has two or more clearly marked lanes for traveling in the same direction,","role":"condition"},{"id":"k4","text":"a driver may not continue to operate a motor vehicle in the extreme left lane","role":"obligation"},{"id":"k5","text":"if the driver knows, or reasonably should know, that he or she is traveling at a rate of speed which is less than the posted speed limit for that portion of the controlled-access highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"k6","text":"and is being overtaken in that lane from the rear by a motor vehicle traveling at a higher rate of speed.","role":"trigger"},{"id":"k8","text":"The requirements of subsection 1 do not apply: (a) To a driver operating a motor vehicle that is:","role":"exception"},{"id":"k9","text":"(1) Overtaking another vehicle proceeding in the same direction;","role":"exception"},{"id":"k10","text":"(2) Preparing for a left turn","role":"exception"},{"id":"k11","text":"at an intersection;","role":"exception"},{"id":"k12","text":"(3) Traveling in a lane designated for the use of high-occupancy vehicles pursuant to NRS 484A.460,","role":"exception"},{"id":"k13","text":"if the driver complies with the requirements to travel in such a lane [DEF-NRS-484A-460-2, NRS-484B-323-1]","role":"reference"},{"id":"k14","text":"or (4) Engaged in the construction, maintenance or repair of the highway, including, without limitation, the removal of snow.","role":"exception"},{"id":"k15","text":"(b) When traffic conditions, inclement weather, obstructions or hazards","role":"exception"},{"id":"k16","text":"make it necessary to drive in the extreme left lane.","role":"standard"},{"id":"k17","text":"(c) When compliance with an official traffic control device or the directions given by a peace officer makes it necessary to drive in the extreme left lane.","role":"exception"},{"id":"k18","text":"(d) To the driver of an authorized emergency vehicle in the course of his or her official duties.","role":"exception"},{"id":"k19","text":"(e) To a driver operating a motor vehicle","role":"exception"},{"id":"k20","text":"within the geographical limits of a city or town.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"k2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.controlled_access"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.controlled_access: 'a highway with access only at designated points, and its entrance and exit lanes', DEF-NRS-484A-060's controlled-access highway; rel.occupies (which lists 'controlled-access lane') anchors it to the subject's footprint."},{"span":"k3","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency"],"derived":[],"justification":"'two or more … lanes for traveling in the same direction': st.lane_adjacency, 'the count of lanes in that direction', at least the stated figure, read on the lane (st.lane) the subject occupies (rel.occupies). 'clearly marked': the lanes' presence on the map is the evidence (observable_reading status)."},{"span":"k4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle","rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a motor vehicle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle. 'in the extreme left lane': st.lane_adjacency, 'ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane, looking along the lane's direction', of the lane the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.lane). 'continue to operate' is the subject remaining there while the triggers hold, over the move-over window; 'driver' and 'operate' are read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"k5","atoms":["kin.speed","dev.speed_limit_sign","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traveling at a rate of speed which is less than the posted speed limit for that portion': kin.speed below the value of a dev.speed_limit_sign ('sign stating a maximum or minimum speed, with value and unit'; kind maximum) that governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls') a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies): the limit of that portion. Same anchoring as 'unless a different speed limit is posted' (LVMC_11_16_060). 'knows, or reasonably should know' is read through those facts themselves (observable_reading perception)."},{"span":"k6","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","kin.speed","prim.closest_approach_within"],"derived":[],"justification":"'being overtaken in that lane from the rear by a motor vehicle': a road user c, a motor vehicle (DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle), behind the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane, 'a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane'); 'traveling at a higher rate of speed': kin.speed of c above the subject's; 'being overtaken': c closes on the subject within a horizon (prim.closest_approach_within, 'under constant velocities, the centres … approach each other at some time between the observation and the horizon'; used for closing only, not for contact or danger)."},{"span":"k8","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a driver operating a motor vehicle that is:' introduces the exceptions (1)-(4) for the subject, a motor vehicle (DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle), carried by their own spans."},{"span":"k9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"],"justification":"'Overtaking another vehicle proceeding in the same direction': drv.interaction.overtake_pass, 'Road user a overtakes and passes road user b from the rear: a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it', with b a vehicle (DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle); the overtaking is under way where its recognition falls within the window ahead of length p.overtake_window."},{"span":"k11","atoms":["st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'at an intersection': st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet', DEF-NRS-484A-105's intersection; it is the target region at which the declared intention is read, bound by the intention's region quantifier."},{"span":"k12","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.reserved_lane"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a lane designated for the use of high-occupancy vehicles': st.reserved_lane, 'lane reserved for a class of vehicles; class ∈ {high_occupancy, …}', class high_occupancy, occupied by the subject (rel.occupies). 'high-occupancy vehicles' borrows DEF-NRS-484A-460-2: '(a) A vehicle that is transporting more than one person; (b) A motorcycle, regardless of the number of passengers; (c) A bus, regardless of the number of passengers; and (d) Any other vehicle designated by regulation.' — the class for which the lane is reserved. 'designated … pursuant to NRS 484A.460' is read through the reserved lane's presence (observable_reading status).","source_spans":["k13"]},{"span":"k14","atoms":["ru.official_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Engaged in the construction, maintenance or repair of the highway, including … the removal of snow': ru.official_vehicle, 'a vehicle in official or contracted road service, identifiable by livery or equipment', kind highway_maintenance; its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: an emergency vehicle' does not apply. Being engaged in the work is read through the vehicle's being such a vehicle (observable_reading purpose). Same atom as 'Any vehicle that is being used in connection with maintenance of the right-of-way' (LVMC_11_27_010_A)."},{"span":"k15","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency","env.precipitation","env.wet_road","env.ice_or_snow","env.visibility","st.obstruction","st.region_geometry","prim.region_lateral_offset"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic conditions': road users of the traffic (DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) occupying (rel.occupies) the lane to the right of the subject's (st.lane, st.lane_adjacency 'left / right neighbouring lane of the same direction'). 'inclement weather': env.precipitation ('rain or snow falling'), env.wet_road, env.ice_or_snow, env.visibility ('visibility distance (fog, dust, smoke)'). 'obstructions or hazards': st.obstruction ('a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user'), located from the subject by its ground distance (st.region_geometry) and its side (prim.region_lateral_offset, 'left positive'), never by a region-to-region relation."},{"span":"k17","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.lane_control_signal","dev.regulatory_sign","dev.temporary_traffic_control","dev.human_direction","rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency"],"derived":[],"justification":"'compliance with an official traffic control device … makes it necessary': a device governing (dev.governs) the lane to the subject's right (st.lane_adjacency) closes it: dev.lane_control_signal state red_x or yellow_x, dev.regulatory_sign code closed_to_traffic or do_not_enter, or dev.temporary_traffic_control ('cones, barricades … marking works, a closure'). 'the directions given by a peace officer': dev.human_direction role police_officer, indication stop, governing that lane. 'official' is read through the device's presence (observable_reading status)."},{"span":"k18","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'authorized emergency vehicle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle, carried by ru.aggregate; being 'in the course of his or her official duties' is read through the vehicle's operation as such (observable_reading purpose)."},{"span":"k19","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a driver operating a motor vehicle': the subject, DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle, read through the vehicle's controlled motion."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"k16","standard":"make it necessary to drive in the extreme left lane","concepts":["rel.surface_gap","kin.speed","env.visibility","st.region_geometry"],"params":["p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice","p.following_decel_dry","p.following_decel_wet","p.following_decel_ice"],"convention":"Stopping-distance convention: S = speed(subject) × H + speed(subject)² / (2 × D), with H and D selected by the surface (_ice where env.ice_or_snow, _wet where env.wet_road or env.precipitation, else _dry), as for following distance. The left lane is necessary where moving right cannot be done within S: a traffic member occupying the right neighbouring lane has a longitudinal body gap to the subject (rel.surface_gap) below S, or an obstruction lies within ground distance S of the subject on its right (st.region_geometry, prim.region_lateral_offset negative), or the visibility distance (env.visibility) is below S. Each factor enters by degree: the subject's speed and the surface move S; the gap, the distance and the visibility are compared with it.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"k20","id":"asm.within_city_or_town_limits","meaning":"the place of the road user at the observation lies within the geographical limits of an incorporated city or of a town, as the map's reading classifies the area"}],"intentions":[{"span":"k10","id":"int.left_turn","meaning":"the source's current plan for the road user includes a turn to the left at the target region, the plan's preparation for that turn included"}],"compositions":[{"span":"k13","as":"definition","source":"DEF-NRS-484A-460-2","quote":"(a) A vehicle that is transporting more than one person; (b) A motorcycle, regardless of the number of passengers; (c) A bus, regardless of the number of passengers; and (d) Any other vehicle designated by regulation."},{"span":"k13","rule":"NRS_484B_323_1","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"compliance"}],"residues":[{"span":"k1","why":"Points to subsection 2, which is appended to this same law line and carried by its own exception spans k8-k20; the duty is the same whether or not these words are read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a motor vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle) occupying a controlled-access highway (rel.occupies, st.controlled_access) and a lane (st.lane) that is the leftmost (st.lane_adjacency ordinal first) of two or more lanes in its direction (st.lane_adjacency count at least two); it is not an authorized emergency vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle), and the reading does not place it within the limits of a city or town (not asm.within_city_or_town_limits).","obligation":"Let S hold at an observation where: the subject occupies the leftmost lane of two or more in its direction on a controlled-access highway; its speed is below the value of some maximum dev.speed_limit_sign governing a travel region it occupies; and none of these holds: (1) within the window ahead of length p.overtake_window, drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, c, p.overtake_window, p.overtake_same_direction_cos) for some vehicle c; (2) intent int.left_turn of the subject at some intersection region; (3) the subject occupies a reserved lane of class high_occupancy and complies with NRS_484B_323_1; (4) the subject is an official vehicle of kind highway_maintenance; (b) with S_stop = speed × H + speed² / (2 × D) (H, D selected by surface as in the operationalization), some traffic member occupies the lane to the right of the subject's lane with longitudinal surface gap below S_stop, or some obstruction lies within ground distance S_stop on the subject's right, or env.visibility is below S_stop; (c) a device governing the lane to the right closes it (lane control signal red_x or yellow_x, regulatory sign closed_to_traffic or do_not_enter, temporary traffic control, or police_officer direction stop). Let O hold where some motor vehicle c is behind the subject in its lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with speed above the subject's and prim.closest_approach_within(subject, c, p.overtaken_closure_horizon). Violated at an observation where, at every observation of the window behind of length p.left_lane_move_over_time, S has held at every observation since an observation at which O and S held together (holdsFor of since(S, O ∧ S)), and some motor vehicle is behind the subject in its lane at the judged observation.","params":["p.left_lane_move_over_time","p.overtaken_closure_horizon","p.overtake_window","p.overtake_same_direction_cos","p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice","p.following_decel_dry","p.following_decel_wet","p.following_decel_ice"],"narrowings":[{"span":"k3","why":"'clearly marked' lanes are read through the lanes the map represents; the paint's clarity is not modelled.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"k4","why":"'continue to operate' is read as the subject remaining in the leftmost lane, slower than the limit and unexcused, for the window p.left_lane_move_over_time after a faster motor vehicle closed on it from behind, with a motor vehicle still behind it in that lane; 'driver' and 'operate' are read through the vehicle's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"k5","why":"'knows, or reasonably should know' is read through the facts known: the subject's own speed and the posted maximum governing where it is.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"perception"},{"span":"k6","why":"'being overtaken' is read as a faster motor vehicle behind in the same lane closing on the subject within p.overtaken_closure_horizon; a faster vehicle farther back is not yet overtaking.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"k12","why":"The lane's designation pursuant to NRS 484A.460 is read through the reserved lane of class high_occupancy the map represents.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"k14","why":"Being engaged in construction, maintenance or repair of the highway is read through the vehicle being a highway-maintenance vehicle in road service.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"},{"span":"k16","why":"'traffic conditions' and 'hazards' are read only through road users in the right neighbouring lane and obstructions on the subject's right; inclement weather only through the surface condition, falling rain and the visibility distance.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"k17","why":"An 'official' device is read through its presence on the road.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"k18","why":"'in the course of his or her official duties' is read through the vehicle's operation as an authorized emergency vehicle; off-duty use is not told apart.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Three-lane controlled-access highway outside city limits (asm.within_city_or_town_limits false), dry; a maximum speed sign of 29 m/s governs the lanes. The subject car drives in the leftmost lane at 24 m/s; a car approaches from 80 m behind in the same lane at 32 m/s, closes and then follows at 24 m/s; the subject stays in the leftmost lane for 30 s with the middle lane empty."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; the subject signals and moves to the middle lane 5 s after the faster car closes from behind."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject car drives in the middle lane at 24 m/s with a faster car behind it."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Same scene as forbid; the source declares dev.speed_limit_sign absent, so whether the subject is below the posted limit is unknown.","masked":["dev.speed_limit_sign"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"Same scene with the reading placing the highway within city limits (asm.within_city_or_town_limits true)."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; a lane control signal showing red_x governs the middle lane throughout, closing it."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject drives in the leftmost lane at 24 m/s with no other road user in the scene."},{"name":"branch_4","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject is an authorized emergency vehicle driving in the leftmost lane at 24 m/s with a faster car closing from behind."},{"name":"branch_5","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; the middle lane is occupied by a truck travelling alongside the subject at a body gap of 5 m throughout, so moving right is not possible."}],"literals":[{"span":"k3","text":"two","value":2,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_lane_move_over_time","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"the time a driver needs, once a faster vehicle closes from behind, to check the mirrors, signal and move one lane to the right: a perception-reaction time, a few seconds of signal and the lane change","source":"lane-change duration studies; driver manuals (signal at least 3 s before a lane change)"},{"name":"p.overtaken_closure_horizon","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"the time ahead within which a faster vehicle closing from behind in the same lane reaches the vehicle ahead under constant velocities, so that it counts as overtaking rather than merely travelling faster far behind","source":"mirror-check intervals of highway driving"},{"name":"p.overtake_window","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind","source":"passing-manoeuvre durations, AASHTO passing sight distance"},{"name":"p.overtake_same_direction_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other","source":"lane-change heading angles"},{"name":"p.following_headway_dry","unit":"s","value":2.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on a dry surface: the two-second rule of driver manuals","source":"state driver handbooks"},{"name":"p.following_headway_wet","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on a wet surface or in rain: the two-second rule lengthened by a second","source":"state driver handbooks"},{"name":"p.following_headway_ice","unit":"s","value":6.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on an icy or snow-covered surface: the tripled following time driver manuals advise","source":"state driver handbooks"},{"name":"p.following_decel_dry","unit":"m/s^2","value":6.0,"convention":"braking deceleration of a passenger vehicle on a dry paved surface (coefficient of friction about 0.6)","source":"AASHTO Green Book; tyre-road friction tables"},{"name":"p.following_decel_wet","unit":"m/s^2","value":4.0,"convention":"braking deceleration of a passenger vehicle on a wet paved surface (coefficient of friction about 0.4)","source":"AASHTO Green Book; tyre-road friction tables"},{"name":"p.following_decel_ice","unit":"m/s^2","value":1.0,"convention":"braking deceleration of a passenger vehicle on an icy or snow-covered surface (coefficient of friction about 0.1)","source":"tyre-road friction tables"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}

