 or the geometric centre, dividing the two directions of a two-way roadway', of the way the subject is on (st.on_way, 'the public way … a structure region lies on'). 'give to the other': the subject's body stays on its own half: prim.region_lateral_offset of the centre line from the subject ('signed lateral offset … left positive') is at least half the subject's full width (kin.extent). 'the other' is the oncoming vehicle met: it closes on the subject within a horizon (prim.closest_approach_within, centres under constant velocities, not a contact or clearance) or is alongside (rel.longitudinal_overlap)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"h6","standard":"as nearly as possible","concepts":["prim.region_lateral_offset","st.road_edge","st.region_geometry"],"params":["p.lateral_position_tolerance"],"convention":"The subject gives the other half of the paved portion as nearly as possible where its body crosses the centre line by no more than a lateral positioning tolerance p.lateral_position_tolerance, or where its body is already within that tolerance of the road edge on its right (st.road_edge, ground distance through st.region_geometry, on the right per prim.region_lateral_offset), so that no more room is available to it.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a vehicle that is not at rest (not drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance), occupying a highway (rel.occupies, st.highway) and a lane (st.lane) whose lane count in its direction (st.lane_adjacency count) is at most one.","obligation":"For every road user c that is a vehicle, occupies the highway the subject occupies, is oncoming to the subject (rel.oncoming with p.oncoming_heading_cos) and is meeting it (prim.closest_approach_within(subject, c, p.meeting_horizon) or rel.longitudinal_overlap: projections share length), and for every centre line l lying on that highway (st.centre_line, st.on_way): prim.region_lateral_offset(l, subject) is at least half the subject's full width (kin.extent) less p.lateral_position_tolerance, or the subject's body is within p.lateral_position_tolerance of a road edge (st.road_edge, st.region_geometry distance) lying on its right (prim.region_lateral_offset negative). Violated where neither holds.","params":["p.oncoming_heading_cos","p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.meeting_horizon","p.lateral_position_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"h1","why":"'Drivers' is read through the vehicles' controlled motion, whoever or whatever controls them.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"h5","why":"'the paved portion of the highway' is read as the roadway the centre line divides; a paved shoulder is not added to either half. Its half is given while the other vehicle approaches within p.meeting_horizon or is alongside.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"h6","why":"'as nearly as possible' is read through the subject's room to its right road edge; obstacles on the subject's half are not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Two-lane two-way road; the moving subject car straddles the centre line by 1 m while an oncoming car approaches 2 s away, with 2 m of room to its right road edge."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same road; the subject car keeps its body right of the centre line as the oncoming car passes."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject car drives on a highway whose lane counts two lanes in its direction."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Two-lane road with an oncoming car approaching; the source maps regions without their outline (st.region_geometry absent), so the offset from the centre line is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject car drives over the centre line on a two-lane road with no other vehicle in the scene."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A very narrow paved road; the subject's body crosses the centre line by 0.5 m while its right side is at the road edge, as an oncoming car passes."}],"literals":[{"span":"h4","text":"one","value":1,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.oncoming_heading_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle off exactly opposed headings (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as proceeding in opposite directions","source":"heading tolerance of road-geometry alignment; lane-change heading angles"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of the acquisition source"},{"name":"p.meeting_horizon","unit":"s","value":5.0,"convention":"the time ahead within which two vehicles closing head-on on a narrow two-way road count as meeting, so that each keeps to its half: the decision-and-steering time of a driver adjusting lateral position","source":"AASHTO decision sight distance (avoidance manoeuvre times)"},{"name":"p.lateral_position_tolerance","unit":"m","value":0.3,"convention":"the lateral margin within which a vehicle body counts as at a line or an edge: lane-keeping variability of a driven vehicle plus the source's position error","source":"lane-keeping lateral deviation studies"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_208_1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-208-1"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"k1","text":"Except as otherwise provided in subsection 2,","role":"exception"},{"id":"k2","text":"on a controlled-access highway","role":"condition"},{"id":"k3","text":"which has two or more clearly marked lanes for traveling in the same direction,","role":"condition"},{"id":"k4","text":"a driver may not continue to operate a motor vehicle in the extreme left lane","role":"obligation"},{"id":"k5","text":"if the driver knows, or reasonably should know, that he or she is traveling at a rate of speed which is less than the posted speed limit for that portion of the controlled-access highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"k6","text":"and is being overtaken in that lane from the rear by a motor vehicle traveling at a higher rate of speed.","role":"trigger"},{"id":"k8","text":"The requirements of subsection 1 do not apply: (a) To a driver operating a motor vehicle that is:","role":"exception"},{"id":"k9","text":"(1) Overtaking another vehicle proceeding in the same direction;","role":"exception"},{"id":"k10","text":"(2) Preparing for a left turn","role":"exception"},{"id":"k11","text":"at an intersection;","role":"exception"},{"id":"k12","text":"(3) Traveling in a lane designated for the use of high-occupancy vehicles pursuant to NRS 484A.460,","role":"exception"},{"id":"k13a","text":"if the driver complies with the requirements to travel in such a lane","role":"exception"},{"id":"k13b","text":"[DEF-NRS-484A-460-2, NRS-484B-323-1]","role":"reference"},{"id":"k14","text":"or (4) Engaged in the construction, maintenance or repair of the highway, including, without limitation, the removal of snow.","role":"exception"},{"id":"k15","text":"(b) When traffic conditions, inclement weather, obstructions or hazards","role":"exception"},{"id":"k16","text":"make it necessary to drive in the extreme left lane.","role":"standard"},{"id":"k17","text":"(c) When compliance with an official traffic control device or the directions given by a peace officer makes it necessary to drive in the extreme left lane.","role":"exception"},{"id":"k18","text":"(d) To the driver of an authorized emergency vehicle in the course of his or her official duties.","role":"exception"},{"id":"k19","text":"(e) To a driver operating a motor vehicle","role":"exception"},{"id":"k20","text":"within the geographical limits of a city or town.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"k2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.controlled_access"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.controlled_access: 'a highway with access only at designated points, and its entrance and exit lanes', DEF-NRS-484A-060's controlled-access highway; rel.occupies (which lists 'controlled-access lane') anchors it to the subject's footprint."},{"span":"k3","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency"],"derived":[],"justification":"'two or more … lanes for traveling in the same direction': st.lane_adjacency, 'the count of lanes in that direction', at least the stated figure, read on the lane (st.lane) the subject occupies (rel.occupies). 'clearly marked': the lanes' presence on the map is the evidence (observable_reading status)."},{"span":"k4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle","rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a motor vehicle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle. 'in the extreme left lane': st.lane_adjacency, 'ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane, looking along the lane's direction', of the lane the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.lane). 'continue to operate' is the subject remaining there while the triggers hold, over the move-over window; 'driver' and 'operate' are read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"k5","atoms":["kin.speed","dev.speed_limit_sign","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traveling at a rate of speed which is less than the posted speed limit for that portion': kin.speed below the value of a dev.speed_limit_sign ('sign stating a maximum or minimum speed, with value and unit'; kind maximum) that governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls') a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies): the limit of that portion. Same anchoring as 'unless a different speed limit is posted' (LVMC_11_16_060). 'knows, or reasonably should know' is read through those facts themselves (observable_reading perception)."},{"span":"k6","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"'being overtaken in that lane from the rear by a motor vehicle': a road user c, a motor vehicle (DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle), behind the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane, 'a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane, along the lane direction'); 'traveling at a higher rate of speed': kin.speed of c above the subject's, so that c, behind in that lane, closes on the subject from the rear: the words read as they say."},{"span":"k8","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a driver operating a motor vehicle that is:' introduces the exceptions (1)-(4) for the subject, a motor vehicle (DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle), carried by their own spans."},{"span":"k9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"],"justification":"'Overtaking another vehicle proceeding in the same direction': drv.interaction.overtake_pass, 'Road user a overtakes and passes road user b from the rear: a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it', with b a vehicle (DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle); the overtaking is under way where its recognition falls within the window ahead of length p.overtake_window."},{"span":"k11","atoms":["st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'at an intersection': st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet', DEF-NRS-484A-105's intersection; it is the target region at which the declared intention is read, bound by the intention's region quantifier."},{"span":"k12","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.reserved_lane"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a lane designated for the use of high-occupancy vehicles': st.reserved_lane, 'lane reserved for a class of vehicles; class ∈ {high_occupancy, …}', class high_occupancy, occupied by the subject (rel.occupies). 'high-occupancy vehicles' borrows DEF-NRS-484A-460-2: '(a) A vehicle that is transporting more than one person; (b) A motorcycle, regardless of the number of passengers; (c) A bus, regardless of the number of passengers; and (d) Any other vehicle designated by regulation.' — the class for which the lane is reserved. 'designated … pursuant to NRS 484A.460' is read through the reserved lane's presence (observable_reading status).","source_spans":["k13b"]},{"span":"k13a","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-460-2::high_occupancy_vehicle","dev.zone_sign","dev.governs","prim.conditions_hold"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the requirements to travel in such a lane' are, by DEF-NRS-484A-460-2, the conditions the Department determines ('(1) The number of occupants required per vehicle; and (2) The hours of the day that the use of the lane is restricted') and advises on signs; the class of road user the lane serves is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-460-2::high_occupancy_vehicle, which borrows '(a) A vehicle that is transporting more than one person; (b) A motorcycle, regardless of the number of passengers; (c) A bus, regardless of the number of passengers; and (d) Any other vehicle designated by regulation.' The posted conditions are a dev.zone_sign of kind high_occupancy_lane governing (dev.governs) the reserved lane, its 'conditions attribute: a structured reading of the sign's legend'; that they hold for the subject is prim.conditions_hold, 'the structured conditions of a device … hold at the observation for a road user'. The sign's exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: whether the condition holds now' is met by reading prim.conditions_hold for it.","source_spans":["k13b"]},{"span":"k14","atoms":["ru.official_vehicle","sig.warning_lamp"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Engaged in the construction, maintenance or repair of the highway, including … the removal of snow': the vehicle is in road service, ru.official_vehicle ('a vehicle in official or contracted road service, identifiable by livery or equipment'), kind highway_maintenance, and shows the conduct of a vehicle at work on the highway: an amber warning lamp lit, flashing or rotating (sig.warning_lamp, 'a warning lamp lit; colour ∈ {red, blue, amber, white}, mode ∈ {flashing, rotating, steady}'). Its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: an audible warning' does not apply; the class's exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: an emergency vehicle' does not apply."},{"span":"k15","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency","env.precipitation","env.wet_road","env.ice_or_snow","env.visibility","st.obstruction","st.region_geometry","prim.region_lateral_offset"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic conditions': road users of the traffic (DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) occupying (rel.occupies) the lane to the right of the subject's (st.lane, st.lane_adjacency 'left / right neighbouring lane of the same direction'). 'inclement weather': env.precipitation ('rain or snow falling'), env.wet_road, env.ice_or_snow, env.visibility ('visibility distance (fog, dust, smoke)'). 'obstructions or hazards': st.obstruction ('a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user'), located from the subject by its ground distance (st.region_geometry) and its side (prim.region_lateral_offset, 'left positive'), never by a region-to-region relation."},{"span":"k17","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.lane_control_signal","dev.regulatory_sign","dev.temporary_traffic_control","dev.human_direction","rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency"],"derived":[],"justification":"'compliance with an official traffic control device … makes it necessary': a device governing (dev.governs) the lane to the subject's right (st.lane_adjacency) closes it: dev.lane_control_signal state red_x or yellow_x, dev.regulatory_sign code closed_to_traffic or do_not_enter, or dev.temporary_traffic_control ('cones, barricades … marking works, a closure'). 'the directions given by a peace officer': dev.human_direction role police_officer, indication stop, governing that lane. 'official' is read through the device's presence (observable_reading status)."},{"span":"k18","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle","sig.warning_lamp","sig.siren"],"derived":[],"justification":"'authorized emergency vehicle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle, carried by ru.aggregate; the class alone is no conduct, so being 'in the course of his or her official duties' is read through the conduct of a vehicle operated on duty as an emergency vehicle: a warning lamp lit, flashing or rotating (sig.warning_lamp, 'a warning lamp lit … mode ∈ {flashing, rotating, steady}') or a siren sounding (sig.siren, 'a siren, whistle or bell sounding'); the source reads the two separately, as sig.siren's contract requires."},{"span":"k19","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a driver operating a motor vehicle': the subject, DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle, read through the vehicle's controlled motion."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"k16","standard":"make it necessary to drive in the extreme left lane","concepts":["rel.surface_gap","kin.speed","env.visibility","st.region_geometry"],"params":["p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice","p.following_decel_dry","p.following_decel_wet","p.following_decel_ice"],"convention":"Stopping-distance convention: S = speed(subject) × H + speed(subject)² / (2 × D), with H and D selected by the surface (_ice where env.ice_or_snow, _wet where env.wet_road or env.precipitation, else _dry), as for following distance. The left lane is necessary where moving right cannot be done within S: a traffic member occupying the right neighbouring lane has a longitudinal body gap to the subject (rel.surface_gap) below S, or an obstruction lies within ground distance S of the subject on its right (st.region_geometry, prim.region_lateral_offset negative), or the visibility distance (env.visibility) is below S. Each factor enters by degree: the subject's speed and the surface move S; the gap, the distance and the visibility are compared with it.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"k20","id":"asm.within_city_or_town_limits","meaning":"the place of the road user at the observation lies within the geographical limits of an incorporated city or of a town, as the map's reading classifies the area"}],"intentions":[{"span":"k10","id":"int.left_turn","meaning":"the source's current plan for the road user includes a turn to the left at the target region, the plan's preparation for that turn included"}],"compositions":[{"span":"k13b","as":"definition","source":"DEF-NRS-484A-460-2","quote":"(a) A vehicle that is transporting more than one person; (b) A motorcycle, regardless of the number of passengers; (c) A bus, regardless of the number of passengers; and (d) Any other vehicle designated by regulation."}],"residues":[{"span":"k1","why":"Points to subsection 2, which is appended to this same law line and carried by its own exception spans k8-k20; the duty is the same whether or not these words are read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a motor vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle) occupying a controlled-access highway (rel.occupies, st.controlled_access) and a lane (st.lane) that is the leftmost (st.lane_adjacency ordinal first) of two or more lanes in its direction (st.lane_adjacency count at least two); it is not an authorized emergency vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle) showing a lit flashing or rotating warning lamp (sig.warning_lamp) or sounding a siren (sig.siren), and the reading does not place it within the limits of a city or town (not asm.within_city_or_town_limits).","obligation":"Let S hold at an observation where: the subject occupies the leftmost lane of two or more in its direction on a controlled-access highway; its speed is below the value of some maximum dev.speed_limit_sign governing a travel region it occupies; and none of these holds: (1) within the window ahead of length p.overtake_window, drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, c, p.overtake_window, p.overtake_same_direction_cos) for some vehicle c; (2) intent int.left_turn of the subject at some intersection region; (3) the subject occupies a reserved lane r of class high_occupancy, is a high-occupancy vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-460-2::high_occupancy_vehicle), and prim.conditions_hold(z, subject) for every dev.zone_sign z of kind high_occupancy_lane governing r; (4) the subject is an official vehicle of kind highway_maintenance showing a lit amber warning lamp, flashing or rotating (sig.warning_lamp); (b) with S_stop = speed × H + speed² / (2 × D) (H, D selected by surface as in the operationalization), some traffic member occupies the lane to the right of the subject's lane with longitudinal surface gap below S_stop, or some obstruction lies within ground distance S_stop on the subject's right, or env.visibility is below S_stop; (c) a device governing the lane to the right closes it (lane control signal red_x or yellow_x, regulatory sign closed_to_traffic or do_not_enter, temporary traffic control, or police_officer direction stop). Let O hold where some motor vehicle c is behind the subject in its lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with speed above the subject's. Violated at an observation where, at every observation of the window behind of length p.left_lane_move_over_time, S has held at every observation since an observation at which O and S held together (holdsFor of since(S, O ∧ S)), and some motor vehicle is behind the subject in its lane at the judged observation.","params":["p.left_lane_move_over_time","p.overtake_window","p.overtake_same_direction_cos","p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice","p.following_decel_dry","p.following_decel_wet","p.following_decel_ice"],"narrowings":[{"span":"k3","why":"'clearly marked' lanes are read through the lanes the map represents; the paint's clarity is not modelled.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"k4","why":"'continue to operate' is read as the subject remaining in the leftmost lane, slower than the limit and unexcused, for the window p.left_lane_move_over_time after a faster motor vehicle closed on it from behind, with a motor vehicle still behind it in that lane; 'driver' and 'operate' are read through the vehicle's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"k5","why":"'knows, or reasonably should know' is read through the facts known: the subject's own speed and the posted maximum governing where it is.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"perception"},{"span":"k6","why":"'being overtaken' is read as a faster motor vehicle behind in the same lane closing on the subject within p.overtaken_closure_horizon; a faster vehicle farther back is not yet overtaking.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"k12","why":"The lane's designation pursuant to NRS 484A.460 is read through the reserved lane of class high_occupancy the map represents.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"k14","why":"Being engaged in construction, maintenance or repair of the highway is read through the vehicle being a highway-maintenance vehicle in road service.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"},{"span":"k16","why":"'traffic conditions' and 'hazards' are read only through road users in the right neighbouring lane and obstructions on the subject's right; inclement weather only through the surface condition, falling rain and the visibility distance.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"k17","why":"An 'official' device is read through its presence on the road.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"k18","why":"'in the course of his or her official duties' is read through the vehicle's operation as an authorized emergency vehicle; off-duty use is not told apart.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Three-lane controlled-access highway outside city limits (asm.within_city_or_town_limits false), dry; a maximum speed sign of 29 m/s governs the lanes. The subject car drives in the leftmost lane at 24 m/s; a car approaches from 80 m behind in the same lane at 32 m/s, closes and then follows at 24 m/s; the subject stays in the leftmost lane for 30 s with the middle lane empty."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; the subject signals and moves to the middle lane 5 s after the faster car closes from behind."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject car drives in the middle lane at 24 m/s with a faster car behind it."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Same scene as forbid; the source declares dev.speed_limit_sign absent, so whether the subject is below the posted limit is unknown.","masked":["dev.speed_limit_sign"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"Same scene with the reading placing the highway within city limits (asm.within_city_or_town_limits true)."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; a lane control signal showing red_x governs the middle lane throughout, closing it."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject drives in the leftmost lane at 24 m/s with no other road user in the scene."},{"name":"branch_4","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject is an authorized emergency vehicle driving in the leftmost lane at 24 m/s with a faster car closing from behind."},{"name":"branch_5","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; the middle lane is occupied by a truck travelling alongside the subject at a body gap of 5 m throughout, so moving right is not possible."}],"literals":[{"span":"k3","text":"two","value":2,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_lane_move_over_time","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"the time a driver needs, once a faster vehicle closes from behind, to check the mirrors, signal and move one lane to the right: a perception-reaction time, a few seconds of signal and the lane change","source":"lane-change duration studies; driver manuals (signal at least 3 s before a lane change)"},{"name":"p.overtaken_closure_horizon","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"the time ahead within which a faster vehicle closing from behind in the same lane reaches the vehicle ahead under constant velocities, so that it counts as overtaking rather than merely travelling faster far behind","source":"mirror-check intervals of highway driving"},{"name":"p.overtake_window","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind","source":"passing-manoeuvre durations, AASHTO passing sight distance"},{"name":"p.overtake_same_direction_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other","source":"lane-change heading angles"},{"name":"p.following_headway_dry","unit":"s","value":2.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on a dry surface: the two-second rule of driver manuals","source":"state driver handbooks"},{"name":"p.following_headway_wet","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on a wet surface or in rain: the two-second rule lengthened by a second","source":"state driver handbooks"},{"name":"p.following_headway_ice","unit":"s","value":6.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on an icy or snow-covered surface: the tripled following time driver manuals advise","source":"state driver handbooks"},{"name":"p.following_decel_dry","unit":"m/s^2","value":6.0,"convention":"braking deceleration of a passenger vehicle on a dry paved surface (coefficient of friction about 0.6)","source":"AASHTO Green Book; tyre-road friction tables"},{"name":"p.following_decel_wet","unit":"m/s^2","value":4.0,"convention":"braking deceleration of a passenger vehicle on a wet paved surface (coefficient of friction about 0.4)","source":"AASHTO Green Book; tyre-road friction tables"},{"name":"p.following_decel_ice","unit":"m/s^2","value":1.0,"convention":"braking deceleration of a passenger vehicle on an icy or snow-covered surface (coefficient of friction about 0.1)","source":"tyre-road friction tables"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}

{"node_id":"NRS_484B_117_1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-117-1"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Except as otherwise provided in subsection 2 [(2) appended below],","role":"exception"},{"id":"s2","text":"the driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"s3","text":"shall not drive upon or within any sidewalk area","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s4","text":"except at a permanent or temporary driveway or alley entrance.","role":"exception"},{"id":"s5","text":"A person who violates this subsection is guilty of a misdemeanor.","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s6","text":"The provisions of subsection 1 do not apply to a vehicle that is powered solely by electricity and designed to travel on three wheels when such a vehicle is operated:","role":"exception"},{"id":"s7","text":"(a) As an authorized emergency vehicle;","role":"exception"},{"id":"s8","text":"(b) By an officer or other authorized employee of a law enforcement agency,","role":"exception"},{"id":"s9","text":"as that term is defined in NRS 239C.065 [DEF-NRS-239C-065],","role":"reference"},{"id":"s10","text":"in the course of his or her official duties; or","role":"exception"},{"id":"s11","text":"(c) By a security guard,","role":"exception"},{"id":"s12","text":"as that term is defined in NRS 648.016 [DEF-NRS-648-016],","role":"reference"},{"id":"s13","text":"in the course of his or her official duties.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"s2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate: the atom's literal argument is an aggregate id'; 'vehicle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway'). 'Driver' is no aggregate: the contract excludes 'a relational role such as who drives or controls a vehicle', so the driver is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency). Same words mapped the same way by NRS_484B_113_2 and LVMC_11_20_060_o1."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"rel.occupies: 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (… sidewalk …)' carries 'upon or within'. st.sidewalk: 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line', which is DEF-NRS-484A-240 'that portion of a highway between the curb lines … and the adjacent property lines intended for the use of pedestrians'; its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: a crosswalk' does not apply, the words name the sidewalk area. 'drive' is the vehicle's controlled motion: the vehicle is not at rest, the negation of drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation … speed at or below a tolerance'), whatever controls it."},{"span":"s4","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.driveway_or_alley_entrance"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.driveway_or_alley_entrance: 'private road, alley or driveway meeting the highway'; its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: which of them meets the highway there' does not apply since the words except driveway and alley entrances alike. 'permanent or temporary' admits both, so the kind is read whatever its permanence. rel.occupies anchors it: the vehicle's footprint overlaps the entrance region while on the sidewalk."},{"span":"s6","atoms":["ru.motorcycle","ru.electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only (gap). ru.motorcycle is a 'motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride' and states neither electric propulsion nor that the vehicle is built for three wheels; ru.electric_scooter is 'a standing or seated electric scooter with handlebars' with no wheel count. Neither carries 'powered solely by electricity and designed to travel on three wheels'."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"The table admits 'authorized emergency vehicle' as DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle ('a vehicle permitted to depart from certain traffic laws when equipped and operated in the manner provided by law'); ru.aggregate carries membership. 'Operated as' one is that membership, not a responding role, which the aggregate's contract excludes."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["ru.emergency_vehicle","ru.official_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only (gap). The words name the person operating, by role: an officer or authorized employee of a 'law enforcement agency', borrowed from DEF-NRS-239C-065: '(2) A metropolitan police department; (3) A police department of an incorporated city; or (4) The Department of Public Safety.' ru.emergency_vehicle (kind police) is 'vehicle of a class the jurisdiction designates as emergency' and ru.official_vehicle a vehicle 'in official or contracted road service': both are classes of the vehicle, not the role of the person at its controls.","source_spans":["s9"]},{"span":"s10","atoms":["ru.emergency_vehicle","ru.official_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only (gap). 'in the course of his or her official duties' is whether the officer acts on duty; no atom carries an operator's duty status, and a vehicle class is not it."},{"span":"s11","atoms":["ru.official_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atom only (gap). 'Security guard' borrowed from DEF-NRS-648-016: 'means a person employed as a watchman, guard, security consultant, patrol officer or in any other similar position.' It is the role of the person operating; ru.official_vehicle ('a vehicle in official or contracted road service') is a vehicle class and no security role.","source_spans":["s12"]},{"span":"s13","atoms":["ru.official_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atom only (gap). The guard's being on duty is an operator's duty status, which no atom carries."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"s9","as":"definition","source":"DEF-NRS-239C-065","quote":"(2) A metropolitan police department; (3) A police department of an incorporated city; or (4) The Department of Public Safety."},{"span":"s12","as":"definition","source":"DEF-NRS-648-016","quote":"means a person employed as a watchman, guard, security consultant, patrol officer or in any other similar position."}],"residues":[{"span":"s1","why":"Points to subsection 2, which is appended to this same law line and carried by its own exception spans s6-s13; the duty is the same whether or not these words are read.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose footprint overlaps a sidewalk region (rel.occupies, st.sidewalk), and it is not an electric three-wheeled vehicle operated as an authorized emergency vehicle, by a law-enforcement officer or employee on duty, or by a security guard on duty (s6-s13, carried by the gap atoms).","obligation":"At every observation at which the subject's footprint overlaps a sidewalk region and the subject is not at rest (not drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance), its footprint also overlaps a driveway or alley entrance region (st.driveway_or_alley_entrance); otherwise violated.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s2","why":"'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever or whatever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"s3","why":"'drive' is read as the vehicle not being at rest while on the sidewalk; a vehicle standing still there is not driving at that observation (its earlier motion onto the sidewalk is judged at the observations where it moved).","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A passenger car leaves the roadway mid-block and drives along the sidewalk at 4 m/s, overlapping no driveway or alley entrance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A passenger car crosses the sidewalk at 2 m/s where it overlaps a driveway entrance region, entering a private driveway."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A passenger car drives along the roadway and never overlaps the sidewalk."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A passenger car moves near the curb; the source declares rel.occupies absent, so whether it is on the sidewalk is unknown.","masked":["rel.occupies"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of the acquisition source"}],"gaps":[{"span":"s6","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.electric_three_wheeler` | a vehicle propelled solely by an electric motor and built to travel on three wheels in contact with the ground, whatever the posture of the person at its controls; a class atom on an entity **Not a stand-in for:** a motorcycle or an electric scooter, whose contracts state neither the propulsion nor the wheel count | local","nearest":["ru.motorcycle","ru.electric_scooter"]},{"span":"s8","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.operator_role` | the role in which the person at a vehicle's controls operates it, as the source records it: **role** ∈ {law_enforcement_officer, security_guard, other}; **on_duty** attribute, true where the person operates it in the course of the duties of that role; decides which road users the sidewalk prohibition exempts **Not a stand-in for:** the vehicle's class (`ru.emergency_vehicle`, `ru.official_vehicle`) — an officer may drive an unmarked vehicle and a marked vehicle may be driven off duty | local","nearest":["ru.emergency_vehicle","ru.official_vehicle"]},{"span":"s10","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.operator_role` | the role in which the person at a vehicle's controls operates it, as the source records it: **role** ∈ {law_enforcement_officer, security_guard, other}; **on_duty** attribute, true where the person operates it in the course of the duties of that role; decides which road users the sidewalk prohibition exempts **Not a stand-in for:** the vehicle's class (`ru.emergency_vehicle`, `ru.official_vehicle`) — an officer may drive an unmarked vehicle and a marked vehicle may be driven off duty | local","nearest":["ru.emergency_vehicle","ru.official_vehicle"]},{"span":"s11","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.operator_role` | the role in which the person at a vehicle's controls operates it, as the source records it: **role** ∈ {law_enforcement_officer, security_guard, other}; **on_duty** attribute, true where the person operates it in the course of the duties of that role; decides which road users the sidewalk prohibition exempts **Not a stand-in for:** the vehicle's class (`ru.emergency_vehicle`, `ru.official_vehicle`) — an officer may drive an unmarked vehicle and a marked vehicle may be driven off duty | local","nearest":["ru.official_vehicle"]},{"span":"s13","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.operator_role` | the role in which the person at a vehicle's controls operates it, as the source records it: **role** ∈ {law_enforcement_officer, security_guard, other}; **on_duty** attribute, true where the person operates it in the course of the duties of that role; decides which road users the sidewalk prohibition exempts **Not a stand-in for:** the vehicle's class (`ru.emergency_vehicle`, `ru.official_vehicle`) — an officer may drive an unmarked vehicle and a marked vehicle may be driven off duty | local","nearest":["ru.official_vehicle"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_127_1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-127-1"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"f1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"f2","text":"shall not follow another vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"f3","text":"more closely than is reasonable and prudent, having due regard for the speed of such vehicles and the traffic upon and the condition of the highway.","role":"standard"}],"elements":[{"span":"f1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate'; 'vehicle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. 'Driver' is a relational role the contract excludes from membership; it is read through the vehicle's controlled motion. Same words as 'The driver of a vehicle' (LVMC_11_20_060_o1)."},{"span":"f2","atoms":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'follow another vehicle': rel.ahead_behind_in_lane, 'a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane, along the lane direction', with the other road user ahead of the subject; the other is a vehicle, ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, never a class list."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"f3","standard":"more closely than is reasonable and prudent, having due regard for the speed of such vehicles and the traffic upon and the condition of the highway","concepts":["rel.surface_gap","kin.speed","env.wet_road","env.precipitation","env.ice_or_snow"],"params":["p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice","p.following_decel_dry","p.following_decel_wet","p.following_decel_ice"],"convention":"Car-following stopping-distance convention: the longitudinal component of the body gap to each vehicle ahead in the lane (rel.surface_gap) is at least the subject's speed times a time headway, plus the difference of the two vehicles' braking distances (subject speed squared minus the followed vehicle's speed squared, over twice a braking deceleration). The speeds of both vehicles enter the bound by degree; the condition of the highway selects the headway and the deceleration: icy or snow-covered surface (env.ice_or_snow) the _ice pair, else a wet surface or falling rain (env.wet_road or env.precipitation) the _wet pair, else the _dry pair. Headways from the driver-manual following-time rules; decelerations from tyre-road friction tables.","surrogate":true}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle).","obligation":"For every road user b that is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane): the longitudinal component of rel.surface_gap(subject, b) is at least speed(subject) × H + (speed(subject)² − speed(b)²) / (2 × D), where H and D are p.following_headway_ice and p.following_decel_ice where env.ice_or_snow holds, else p.following_headway_wet and p.following_decel_wet where env.wet_road or env.precipitation holds, else p.following_headway_dry and p.following_decel_dry (written with Term.cond). Violated at an observation where some such b is closer.","params":["p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice","p.following_decel_dry","p.following_decel_wet","p.following_decel_ice"],"narrowings":[{"span":"f1","why":"'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever or whatever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"f3","why":"'the traffic upon … the highway' is read only through the followed vehicle and its speed, the part of the traffic the following distance answers to; the density of other traffic is not read. 'the condition of the highway' is read only through its surface (wet, icy or snow-covered, or rain falling); grade, curvature and surface damage are not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Dry road; the subject car follows another car in its lane, both at 25 m/s, with a body gap of 15 m."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Dry road; the subject car follows another car in its lane, both at 25 m/s, with a body gap of 70 m."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject is a bicycle (a device moved by human power, outside the vehicle aggregate) riding close behind a car."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The subject car follows another car in its lane; the source declares rel.surface_gap absent.","masked":["rel.surface_gap"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject car drives alone on the road: no vehicle is ahead of it in its lane."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"Icy road (env.ice_or_snow true); both cars at 25 m/s with a body gap of 70 m, which meets the dry bound but not the icy one."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.following_headway_dry","unit":"s","value":2.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on a dry surface: the two-second rule of driver manuals","source":"state driver handbooks"},{"name":"p.following_headway_wet","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on a wet surface or in rain: the two-second rule lengthened by a second","source":"state driver handbooks"},{"name":"p.following_headway_ice","unit":"s","value":6.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on an icy or snow-covered surface: the tripled following time driver manuals advise","source":"state driver handbooks"},{"name":"p.following_decel_dry","unit":"m/s^2","value":6.0,"convention":"braking deceleration of a passenger vehicle on a dry paved surface (coefficient of friction about 0.6)","source":"AASHTO Green Book; tyre-road friction tables"},{"name":"p.following_decel_wet","unit":"m/s^2","value":4.0,"convention":"braking deceleration of a passenger vehicle on a wet paved surface (coefficient of friction about 0.4)","source":"AASHTO Green Book; tyre-road friction tables"},{"name":"p.following_decel_ice","unit":"m/s^2","value":1.0,"convention":"braking deceleration of a passenger vehicle on an icy or snow-covered surface (coefficient of friction about 0.1)","source":"tyre-road friction tables"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_127_2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-127-2"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-050::combination_of_vehicles"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"The driver of any truck or combination of vehicles 80 inches or more in overall width,","role":"subject"},{"id":"g2","text":"which is following a truck, or combination of vehicles 80 inches or more in overall width,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"g3","text":"shall, whenever conditions permit,","role":"standard"},{"id":"g4","text":"leave a space of 500 feet so that an overtaking vehicle may enter and occupy such space without danger,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g5","text":"but this shall not prevent a truck or combination of vehicles from overtaking and passing any vehicle or combination of vehicles.","role":"exception"},{"id":"g6","text":"This subsection does not apply to any vehicle or combination of vehicles while moving on a highway on which there are two or more lanes available for traffic moving in the same direction.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"g1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-050::combination_of_vehicles","kin.extent"],"derived":[],"justification":"'truck' and 'combination of vehicles' are admitted aggregates (DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck, 'every motor vehicle which is used for the transportation or delivery of goods with a body built and designed for that purpose'; DEF-NRS-484A-050::combination_of_vehicles, 'two or more vehicles coupled together'), claimed through ru.aggregate. '80 inches or more in overall width': kin.extent, 'the body's size along its axes … a formula reads the full length, width and height', the full width compared with the stated figure. 'Driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"g2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-050::combination_of_vehicles","kin.extent","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane"],"derived":[],"justification":"'following': rel.ahead_behind_in_lane, 'a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane, along the lane direction', the followed road user b ahead of the subject with no other road user between them in that lane (the one it immediately follows). b is a truck or a combination of vehicles (the admitted aggregates) whose full width (kin.extent) is at least the stated figure."},{"span":"g4","atoms":["rel.surface_gap"],"derived":[],"justification":"'leave a space of 500 feet': rel.surface_gap, 'distance between the nearest points of two bodies … its longitudinal and lateral components', the longitudinal component to the followed vehicle at least the stated figure. The words 'so that an overtaking vehicle may enter and occupy such space without danger' state why the space is left; the duty is the stated space itself (narrowing)."},{"span":"g5","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-050::combination_of_vehicles"],"derived":["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"],"justification":"'overtaking and passing any vehicle or combination of vehicles': drv.interaction.overtake_pass, 'Road user a overtakes and passes road user b from the rear … comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it', with a the subject and b any road user that is a vehicle or a combination of vehicles (admitted aggregates). The pass is under way where its recognition falls within the window ahead of length p.overtake_window, the concept's own recognition window."},{"span":"g6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a highway on which there are two or more lanes available for traffic moving in the same direction': st.lane_adjacency, 'lane ordinal within the carriageway and the count of lanes in that direction', read on the lane (st.lane, 'a longitudinal strip of roadway for one line of vehicles') the subject occupies (rel.occupies); the count is at least the stated figure. 'any vehicle or combination of vehicles' is the subject already bound by g1."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"g3","standard":"whenever conditions permit","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","drv.motion.complete_halt"],"params":["p.truck_space_open_time","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"Conditions permit the space where the followed vehicle has been the subject's immediate leader in its lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane, no other road user between) and neither vehicle has been at rest (not drv.motion.complete_halt) at every observation of the window behind of length p.truck_space_open_time: the time a heavy vehicle needs to open the space behind a leader by easing off a few miles per hour. A leader that has just come ahead of the subject, or a queue at rest, does not yet permit it.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-305::truck","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-050::combination_of_vehicles"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a truck or a combination of vehicles (either admitted aggregate) whose full width (kin.extent) is at least 80 inches, and the lane it occupies (rel.occupies, st.lane) does not count two or more lanes in its direction (st.lane_adjacency count).","obligation":"For every road user b that is a truck or a combination of vehicles of full width at least 80 inches, ahead of the subject in its lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with no other road user ahead of the subject and behind b in that lane: either (i) conditions do not permit — it is not the case that, at every observation of the window behind of length p.truck_space_open_time, b was so the subject's immediate leader and neither the subject nor b was at rest (drv.motion.complete_halt, p.halt_speed_tolerance); or (ii) the subject is overtaking and passing — within the window ahead of length p.overtake_window some road user c that is a vehicle or a combination of vehicles is overtaken and passed by the subject (drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, c) with p.overtake_window, p.overtake_same_direction_cos); or (iii) the longitudinal component of rel.surface_gap(subject, b) is at least 500 feet. Violated where none holds.","params":["p.truck_space_open_time","p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.overtake_window","p.overtake_same_direction_cos"],"narrowings":[{"span":"g1","why":"'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the truck's or combination's conduct whoever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"g4","why":"'so that an overtaking vehicle may enter and occupy such space without danger' states the purpose of the space; the duty is the stated space, and whether an overtaking vehicle is present is not read.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"g3","why":"'whenever conditions permit' is a catch-all read only through the leader having been the subject's immediate leader, both moving, for the window that opening the space takes; other conditions (grade, traffic behind) are not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Two-lane two-way highway (one lane each direction); a 2.6 m wide truck follows another 2.6 m wide truck at 60 m, both at 25 m/s, for 60 s with no one between and no overtaking."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same road; the following wide truck keeps a body gap of 200 m to the wide truck ahead."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject is a motorcycle following a wide truck at 30 m."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Two trucks follow each other at 60 m; the source declares kin.extent absent, so neither width is known.","masked":["kin.extent"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The wide trucks travel on a highway whose lane counts two lanes in their direction."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The following wide truck closes to 40 m and, within 8 s, overtakes and passes the leading truck in the opposing lane."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The wide truck drives alone: no road user is ahead of it in its lane."},{"name":"branch_4","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A wide truck pulled into the lane ahead of the subject 5 s ago and is 60 m ahead; the window to open the space has not elapsed."}],"literals":[{"span":"g1","text":"80 inches","value":80,"unit":"in"},{"span":"g2","text":"80 inches","value":80,"unit":"in"},{"span":"g4","text":"500 feet","value":500,"unit":"ft"},{"span":"g6","text":"two","value":2,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.truck_space_open_time","unit":"s","value":30.0,"convention":"the time a following heavy vehicle needs to open a space behind a leader that has come ahead of it, easing off by a few miles per hour: about 150 m at a closing speed near 5 m/s","source":"heavy-vehicle following practice; commercial driver manuals"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of the acquisition source"},{"name":"p.overtake_window","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind","source":"passing-manoeuvre durations, AASHTO passing sight distance"},{"name":"p.overtake_same_direction_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other","source":"lane-change heading angles"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
