{"node_id":"NRS_484B_153_2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-153-2"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"d1","text":"A person","role":"subject"},{"id":"d2","text":"shall not open the door of or board or alight from","role":"obligation"},{"id":"d3","text":"the side of a vehicle which is closest to passing traffic","role":"condition"},{"id":"d4","text":"in such a manner as to interfere with","role":"standard"},{"id":"d5","text":"moving vehicular traffic.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"d1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"The person who opens a door, boards or alights is not observable as such; the conduct is the door of a vehicle opening, so the rule judges the vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose door it is. Same words mapped to the vehicle aggregate by LVMC_11_22_010."},{"span":"d2","atoms":["sig.door_open"],"derived":[],"justification":"sig.door_open: 'a door open; side ∈ {traffic, curb}'. Opening the door, boarding and alighting through that side all show as the door on that side being open."},{"span":"d3","atoms":["sig.door_open","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the side of a vehicle which is closest to passing traffic' is the value side = traffic of sig.door_open; the vehicle is the subject (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle)."},{"span":"d5","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'vehicular traffic': road users that are traffic (admitted DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, 'vehicles and other conveyances … using any highway for purposes of travel') and vehicles (DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle); 'moving': not at rest, the negation of drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation')."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"d4","standard":"in such a manner as to interfere with","conc