), the longitudinal component of rel.surface_gap(subject, b) is at least p.caravan_entry_vehicle_length + 2 × speed(subject) × p.caravan_entry_headway; violated where it is less.","params":["p.caravan_entry_vehicle_length","p.caravan_entry_headway"],"narrowings":[{"span":"c1","why":"'being driven' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, whoever or whatever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Rural highway outside any business district; a motorcade member follows the member ahead at 20 m, both at 25 m/s."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same motorcade; the member keeps a body gap of 150 m to the member ahead at 25 m/s."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The motorcade drives through a business district (asm.business_district true)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Motorcade members on a rural highway; the source declares rel.surface_gap absent.","masked":["rel.surface_gap"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The lead vehicle of the motorcade has no member ahead of it in its lane."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.caravan_entry_vehicle_length","unit":"m","value":22.4,"convention":"overall length of the largest design combination vehicle (an interstate semitrailer) that may enter the space between caravan members","source":"AASHTO Green Book design vehicles (WB-67)"},{"name":"p.caravan_entry_headway","unit":"s","value":2.0,"convention":"time headway kept in front of and behind a vehicle that has entered the space: the two-second rule of driver manuals","source":"state driver handbooks"}],"gaps":[{"span":"c4","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.procession_member` | a road user travelling as a member of an organized group of vehicles proceeding together in a caravan or motorcade, as the source records the group; a **group** attribute identifies the procession, so that two members of one procession are told apart from two vehicles that merely follow each other; decides which road users owe the caravan spacing and between which of them it is measured **Not a stand-in for:** following (`rel.ahead_behind_in_lane`) or travelling in the same direction (`rel.same_direction`) — vehicles following one another in traffic are no procession | general","nearest":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.same_direction"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_153_2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-153-2"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"d1","text":"A person","role":"subject"},{"id":"d2","text":"shall not open the door of or board or alight from","role":"obligation"},{"id":"d3","text":"the side of a vehicle which is closest to passing traffic","role":"condition"},{"id":"d4","text":"in such a manner as to interfere with","role":"standard"},{"id":"d5","text":"moving vehicular traffic.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"d1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"The person who opens a door, boards or alights is not observable as such; the conduct is the door of a vehicle opening, so the rule judges the vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) whose door it is. Same words mapped to the vehicle aggregate by LVMC_11_22_010."},{"span":"d2","atoms":["sig.door_open"],"derived":[],"justification":"sig.door_open: 'a door open; side ∈ {traffic, curb}'. Opening the door, boarding and alighting through that side all show as the door on that side being open."},{"span":"d3","atoms":["sig.door_open","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the side of a vehicle which is closest to passing traffic' is the value side = traffic of sig.door_open; the vehicle is the subject (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle)."},{"span":"d5","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'vehicular traffic': road users that are traffic (admitted DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, 'vehicles and other conveyances … using any highway for purposes of travel') and vehicles (DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle); 'moving': not at rest, the negation of drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation')."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"d4","standard":"in such a manner as to interfere with","concepts":["rel.contact","rel.longitudinal_overlap","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.door_swing_reach"],"convention":"While the traffic-side door is open, a moving vehicle of the traffic is interfered with where it touches the subject (rel.contact) or passes alongside it (rel.longitudinal_overlap: the two projections on the subject's heading share length) with a lateral body gap (rel.surface_gap, lateral component) no greater than the lateral reach of an open side door, p.door_swing_reach: it then drives through the space the open door takes.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a vehicle and its door on the side closest to passing traffic is open (sig.door_open side traffic).","obligation":"No road user c that is traffic and a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and not at rest (not drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance) is in contact with the subject (rel.contact), or alongside it (rel.longitudinal_overlap: projections share length) with the lateral component of rel.surface_gap(subject, c) at most p.door_swing_reach; violated where one is.","params":["p.door_swing_reach","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"d1","why":"'A person' who opens the door, boards or alights is read through the vehicle's traffic-side door being open: who is at the door is not observable.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"d2","why":"Boarding and alighting are read through the open traffic-side door they pass through; boarding or alighting from a vehicle side that has no door is not read.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"d4","why":"Interference is read as a moving vehicle touching the subject or passing alongside within the open door's reach; a moving vehicle that brakes or swerves earlier to avoid the door is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car parked at the curb opens its traffic-side door; a moving car passes alongside it with a lateral body gap of 0.5 m."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car parked at the curb opens its traffic-side door; a moving car passes alongside with a lateral body gap of 2.5 m."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car parked at the curb with all doors closed while traffic passes close by."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A car parked at the curb with traffic passing close by; the source declares sig.door_open absent.","masked":["sig.door_open"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car parked at the curb opens its traffic-side door with no other road user in the scene."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.door_swing_reach","unit":"m","value":1.0,"convention":"lateral reach of an open passenger-car side door beyond the vehicle body (a front door opens about 0.9 to 1.1 m)","source":"vehicle door-opening dimensions; dooring-zone guidance"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of the acquisition source"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
