{"node_id":"NRS_484B_203_1_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-203-1"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"h1","text":"Drivers of vehicles proceeding in opposite directions","role":"subject"},{"id":"h2","text":"shall pass each other keeping to the right,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"h3","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"h4","text":"upon highways having width for not more than one line of traffic in each direction,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"h5","text":"each driver shall give to the other at least one-half of the paved portion of the highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"h6","text":"as nearly as possible.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"h1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","rel.oncoming"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'vehicles' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, for the subject and the other. 'proceeding in opposite directions': rel.oncoming, 'headings opposed and closing', with its tolerance; its exclusion concerns 'the direction a road user approaches from' an intersection, which these words do not name: they name two vehicles meeting on a way. 'proceeding': the subject is not at rest (negation of drv.motion.complete_halt). 'Drivers' is read through the vehicles' controlled motion."},{"span":"h2","atoms":["rel.longitudinal_overlap","rel.bearing","rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pass each other': the two are alongside, rel.longitudinal_overlap, 'the length the two footprints' projections on that axis share'. 'keeping to the right': each keeps the other on its left, rel.bearing, 'direction of b from a in a's frame (for \"on the right of\" …)', its lateral component on the subject's left. Both occupy the same highway (rel.occupies, st.highway, 'the entire public way between its boundary lines'), so a vehicle on another way is not met."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],